\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Orbits and their direction}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{[Topological equivalence](fnip-0082) carries orbits and their
direction.
\citet{p. 45}{kuznetsov2004elements} records that this comparison
keeps the number, the stability, and the topology of the
[invariant sets](fnip-0015), and loses the time-dependent
behavior. A firing frequency is a rate of that kind. The same page
names stronger equivalences, such as orbital and smooth ones, for
that lost information.}
